# 1v1, what opponent memory is worth: every battle cold, then warm on the profile it left (BENCH-175, K3 of the road
# to king). Leigh starts it once the PC is free (not beside another card: two cards on one checkout collide):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-warm        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-warm)
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers, truth log off. Every step resumes; no step needs a
# decision. About 3 h of battles (400 robots x 2 seeds x 3 builds x cold + warm = 4,800).
#
# Why: the bench fights every battle cold, but live clients remember their opponents (3.12's read: a stored
# verdict for about 55% of them), so half the live score is played warm and the bench has never measured it.
# K3 ("round 1 plays the gun the robot has") would ship profiles in the jar so every battle starts warm, which
# only pays if warm beats cold. Cloud reads 2026-11-02 (docs/bench/k3-warm.md):
#   - 3.21 warm on its own stats-only profile (as live clients keep most): +1.36 +- 3.65 points over 24 robots;
#     Neutrino 87 -> 71 (the stored T0 tier fires POW-1's full power and we fire ourselves dry).
#   - with every opponent's KNN seeds kept (seedall, sa): warm lost on all three robots read (Neutrino 85 -> 69,
#     PvP1 89 -> 78, JollyNinja 95 -> 66 in a 5-round smoke). Live clients keep seeds for up to five opponents
#     we score under 60% against (MEM-8), so this is also a possible live leak.
#
# Lukewarm (lw, a lukewarm start before adapting): the stored tier still opens the battle at
# full power (POW-1, POW-3), but once this battle's own hit rate on them is known within POW-4's margin the tier
# rules apply only where POW-4's expected-value check also picks full power. The cold battle is the same as aa's
# (a cold battle has no tier), so lw's cold against aa's cold is a second A/A.
#
# cw:   screen-311.txt (400 robots drawn in proportion to band size, so a mean is an APS estimate) x sa (robot) and
#       aa (baseline, master's A/A build) x 2 fresh seeds from 7900, each cold then warm (--cold-warm).
# lw:   lw on its own, same seeds, each cold then warm; read against cw's aa rows (same battles, same seeds).
# read: per build warm minus cold, sa minus aa warm, the cold pair as an A/A, the robots memory hurts and helps most.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): halt on 30 failed battles, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 200, or no
# battle in 30 minutes; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes. A halt leaves the rest of the step, the
# steps after it and the PR unrun. ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop. Nothing here ships: it decides whether K3 ships profiles
# (warm beats cold), whether memory needs a fix first (warm loses), whether lukewarm is that fix, and which robots
# each applies to.

set V = 3.21
set P = --parallel 12 --no-truth-log
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant 1488498 --child-heap 2G
set W = work/warm
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && bash ./build-ablation.sh seedall && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}sa.jar && bash ./build-ablation.sh lukewarm && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}lw.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set screen-311.txt && mvn -q compile

cw | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set screen-311.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 7900 --robot-jar bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}sa.jar --robot "hadur117.Hadur ${V}sa" --baseline bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}aa.jar --baseline-robot "hadur117.Hadur ${V}aa" --cold-warm --out ${W} --label warm
  after: prep
  stop: fails 30
  stop: skips 60 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

lw | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set screen-311.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 7900 --robot-jar bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}lw.jar --robot "hadur117.Hadur ${V}lw" --cold-warm --out ${W}-lw --label warm-lw
  after: cw
  stop: fails 30
  stop: skips 60 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

read | python3 tools/cold_warm_read.py ${W}/cold-warm.tsv --robot "hadur117.Hadur ${V}sa" --baseline "hadur117.Hadur ${V}aa" --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_warm.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/warm-per-robot.tsv && python3 tools/cold_warm_read.py ${W}/cold-warm.tsv ${W}-lw/cold-warm.tsv --robot "hadur117.Hadur ${V}lw" --baseline "hadur117.Hadur ${V}aa" --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_warm-lw.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/warm-lw-per-robot.tsv
  after: lw

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-warm-results "1v1 opponent memory: cold against warm, with seeds and lukewarm (K3)" ${OUT}/*_warm.md ${OUT}/*_warm-lw.md ${OUT}/warm-per-robot.tsv ${OUT}/warm-lw-per-robot.tsv
  after: read
